Outputs the current '''month''' in Japan Standard Time (JST, UTC+9), via [[Module:JST]]. Use this instead of the built-in <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTMONTH}}</nowiki></code> whenever a date should follow Japan's local time rather than the wiki server clock. Takes no parameters.

==Syntax==
{{T|CURRENTJSTMONTH}}

==Examples==
{{T|CURRENTJSTMONTH|_Y_=1}}

==See also==
Part of the JST date family, all backed by [[Module:JST]]:
* {{T|CURRENTJSTYEAR}} — current year (JST)
* {{T|CURRENTJSTMONTH}} — current month (JST)
* {{T|CURRENTJSTDAY}} — current day of the month (JST)